{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph: an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a member of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":". The vertices are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" and the columns,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hyperedges, are at positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms run on it unchanged; it is not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" even when built from one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because a cell edit can give a column any number of bits."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/Se","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SE","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SH","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix.swift#L28","fileName":"IncidenceMatrix.swift"},"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"}],"title":"IncidenceMatrix"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A column is any set of vertices: empty columns and repeated columns are kept, and a graph’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop is the one bit at its vertex, the hyperedge {v}. (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"loop a zero column; Godsil–Royle’s entry 2 is not a bit. A zero column would forget the loop.)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" is the directed form; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation of the same hypergraphs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Both orientations are stored, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stores its rows: n rows of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"⌈m\/64⌉ words and m columns of ⌈n\/64⌉ words, with the row and column popcounts cached. So","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are each one ","type":"text"},{"code":"BitSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" copy of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and ","type":"text"},{"code":"transposed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the dual,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"swaps the two in O(1). The cost is 2·n·m\/8 bytes: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the matrix is for dense or small"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidence"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (spectral work at n·m up to about 10⁹, hypergraphs with large hyperedges). Sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incidence belongs in ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape: column order is observable, because a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"column’s position is what a spectral caller indexes by. ("},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s equality"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignores positions; convert to compare that way.)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init()","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-4158r","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/In